= MaterialX Fake Window =

#context: vop
#type: node

"""Fakes an interior seen through a window, using five directional maps and no geometry."""

== Overview ==

MaterialX Fake Window walks the incident ray into a virtual box behind the
surface and samples whichever wall the ray reaches, producing the illusion of a
room behind a window without any interior geometry, for Solaris and Karma.

Place it inside a Material Library or MaterialX Builder and connect its output
to the base colour or emission of an mtlxstandard_surface. The surface needs
usable UVs: the room is laid out in UV space, so the effect follows the 0 to 1
square.

All five maps are sampled on every shade. MaterialX cannot switch a filename,
so the wall is chosen after sampling rather than before. If this becomes a
bottleneck, combine the walls into a single atlas.

@parameters

Opposite Map:
    #id: opposite_map
    Texture for the back wall, seen when looking straight through the window.

Left Side Map:
    #id: left_side_map
    Texture for the left wall. Visible when looking in from the right.

Right Side Map:
    #id: right_side_map
    Texture for the right wall. Visible when looking in from the left.

Top Map:
    #id: top_map
    Texture for the ceiling. Visible when looking up from below.

Bottom Map:
    #id: bottom_map
    Texture for the floor. Visible when looking down from above.

Depth:
    #id: depth
    How far the virtual room extends behind the surface, in UV units. Larger
    values give a deeper room and a stronger parallax shift.
